     <item row="3" column="0" colspan="2">
      <layout class="QGridLayout" name="layoutFlags">
       <item row="3" column="0">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagRespawn">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>If this box is checked, then refs that use this Actor Base as their base form will resurrect (unless they start dead) and reset when their parent cell resets.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Respawn</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="4" column="1">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagSimple">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>Simple actors don't use face animations or morphs, and aren't tracked by the Story Manager's &quot;assault&quot; and &quot;death&quot; events.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Simple Actor</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="0" column="1">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagSummonable">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>Control whether this actor can be summoned using a Summon Actor magic effect.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Summonable</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="2" column="0">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagProtected">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>Protected actors cannot be killed by anyone except the player. If their health is brought to or below zero by any other force, they will enter the &quot;bleedout&quot; state instead.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Protected</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="4" column="0">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagUnique">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Unique</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="2" column="1">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagInvulnerable">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>Invulnerable actors are immune to damage. The difference between this and the &quot;Is Ghost&quot; checkbox is that invulnerable actors can still be physically hit by projectiles and attacks; they just take no damage.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Invulnerable</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="3" column="1">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagDoesntBleed">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Doesn't Bleed</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="0" column="0">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagPreset">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>This checkbox doesn't directly make an actor count as a preset usable by the player, but within the Creation Kit, it does influence whether the actor is categorized under &quot;Presets&quot; in the Object Window's tree view.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Is CharGen Preset</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="1" column="0">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagEssential">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>Essential actors are incapable of dying. When their health drops to or below zero, they will enter a state called &quot;bleedout,&quot; where they drop to their knees and are unable to act. They will recover once their health regenerates back above zero. Note that checking this box will make an actor permanently essential; you can make actors temporarily essential using Quest Aliases.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Essential</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="1" column="1">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagGhost">
         <property name="whatsThis">
          <string>If this box is checked, then this actor cannot be struck by weapons or projectiles. Weapons and projectiles will move through them without impacting them or triggering any reaction.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Is Ghost</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item row="5" column="0" colspan="2">
        <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagDoesntAffectStealthMeter">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Doesn't Affect Stealth Meter</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
